  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNICEF CHILD WASTING GAP</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Global Action Plan and the UNICEF&#x2019;s 2022 Acceleration plan 2022, targets priority countries in Horn of Africa, Central Sahel and others impacted by the current food and nutrition crisis. The 15 worst affected countries have an estimated 40 million children under five living in severe food poverty, and 8 million suffering from severe wasting. Ireland&#x2019;s 2023 support to UNICEF will have a particular focus on Democratic Republic of Congo, Madagascar, and Malawi, taking into consideration both the expected needs, and the funding support available in the target countries for a continuum of prevention-detection-treatment of Child Wasting.</narrative>
  </description>
